From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:41:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: defer the vertex/tiler wait on fragment work until
 it matters

Barriers whose second scope names pre-rasterization shader stages (common:
renderers pass all shader stages after rendering to a texture) make the
vertex/tiler subqueue wait for all prior fragment work, so the next
render pass can't start tiling until the previous one is shaded.

When the vertex/tiler side of the second scope is only pre-rasterization
shader stages, record the wait instead of emitting it. Emit it before the
first draw whose vertex-stage shaders access memory (textures, images,
SSBOs, global; flagged at compile time and kept in the shader cache) or
that uses geometry/tessellation, before any barrier where another subqueue
waits on the vertex/tiler one, before events and queries, before executing
secondaries and at the end of the command buffer. The fragment subqueue
still signals. PANVK_NO_LAZY_VT_WAIT=1 disables it.

Hades (Vulkan renderer), Mali-G615 MC6: 502 MHz 48.3 -> 54.7 fps (DDK
58.4), 1255 MHz 103.1 -> 123.9 fps (DDK 132.2). Hades through DXVK
unchanged (99.9 / 100.9 fps at 502 MHz). PanProbe 38/38.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: defer the vertex/tiler wait on fragment work for barriers that only name pre-rasterization shader stages, until a draw whose vertex-stage shaders access memory
Upstream-commit: none (generic PanVK CSF; upstream candidate)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none
Validation test: Hades Vulkan renderer 48.3 -> 54.7 fps at 502 MHz (DDK 58.4), 103.1 -> 123.9 at 1255 MHz (DDK 132.2); Hades DXVK unchanged; PanProbe 38/38; no GPU faults
